.TH MCPICK 1 "2026" "mcpick" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcpick \- choose which MCP servers a session loads, at the moment you launch it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcpick
.RI [ options ]
.B run
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B mcpick
.RI [ options ]
.BR list | doctor | measure | export | serve | import | move | profile
.br
.B mcpick
.RI [ options ]
.BR login | logout
.I server
.br
.BR "mcpick agents" | restore
.SH DESCRIPTION
Coding agents connect to every MCP server they can find and spend context on the
tool definitions whether the session needs them or not.
.B mcpick
puts a checkbox list in front of that: it merges the servers it can see, shows
what each one costs in context, remembers what you picked, and launches the
agent with only the checked ones.
.PP
Nine agents are supported; the Antigravity CLI
.RB ( agy )
is launched unchanged, with a notice. Which mechanism is used depends on what
the agent offers: a command-line flag where one exists, an overlay of the agent's config
directory where a directory variable exists, and a rewrite-and-restore of the
project file otherwise. Run
.B mcpick agents
to see what applies to each.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR...]
Resolve a selection, render a config in the agent's dialect and launch the
command. Everything after
.B run
is passed through untouched.
.TP
.B list
Print the merged catalog. With
.BR \-\-json ,
print it as JSON.
.TP
.B doctor
Connect to each selected server and report tool count, context cost, latency and
the reason for any failure. A stdio server whose command is not trusted is
reported as skipped rather than run; see
.BR \-\-trust .
Exits non-zero if any server is unreachable or skipped.
.TP
.B measure
Connect to every server in the catalog, print what each costs in context, most
expensive first, and cache the numbers for
.BR list .
(The picker measures afresh with \fBm\fR; it never shows a cached number.) A
stdio server's command runs only once trusted, and a remote server the
project's catalog defines is contacted unselected only when its URL and
headers hold no \fB${VAR}\fR or \fB{UUID}\fR, its host is public and no proxy
applies (the address dialled is checked too), or once the catalog is
trusted; see
.BR \-\-trust-catalog .
Servers left out are named on standard error, with what would lift that.
.TP
.B export
Print the selection in an agent's dialect on standard output. The output is
the rendered config, credentials expanded; a warning on standard error says so
when it holds any, and when nothing is selected.
.TP
.B serve
Run mcpick itself as one MCP server fronting the selection, over stdio or, with
.BR \-\-addr ,
over HTTP. Tools are namespaced \fIserver\fB__\fItool\fR.
.TP
.B import
Seed the catalog from
.IR ~/.claude.json .
Credentials written in a spec \(em under a secret-sounding key, as the value
of such a flag or of a \fB\-H\fR header in the arguments, in a URL's
password or query, a token with a well-known prefix, or a
\fBBearer\fR/\fBBasic\fR/\fBToken\fR value under any key \(em are rewritten as \fB${VAR:?export VAR}\fR
references and the variables to export are printed;
.B \-\-yes
copies them as they are, with a warning.
.TP
.B move \fIserver\fR \fBproject\fR|\fBlocal\fR|\fBuser\fR
Move a server between the catalog (\fBproject\fR) and the local and user
servers of \fI~/.claude.json\fR, as \fBv\fR in the picker does. The groups
are named as Claude Code names its scopes. The
destination is written first, then the source; a delete that fails says the
server is now in both files. A name the destination already has is refused;
plugin servers cannot be moved. Into the catalog, a server whose spec holds
credentials written out needs
.B \-\-yes
(write them as they are) or
.B \-\-redact
(write \fB${VAR}\fR references and print what to export); on a terminal the
question is asked, without one the move is refused. A server disabled in
Claude Code stays disabled.
.TP
.B profile \fR[\fBlist\fR | \fBsave\fR \fIname\fR | \fBdelete\fR \fIname\fR | \fBrename\fR \fIold new\fR]
List every profile with its source (yours, the catalog's, the built-in
\fBdefault\fR), save the selection (or \fB\-\-select\fR) as one of yours,
remove or rename one of yours. Yours live in \fI~/.mcpick/profiles.yaml\fR.
A \fBprofiles:\fR key in the catalog is shared: mcpick lists and loads them,
\fBc\fR in the picker copies one into yours, \fBd\fR (or \fBdelete\fR)
deletes it from the file.
.TP
.B login \fIserver\fR
Run the OAuth flow for a remote server: protected-resource discovery, dynamic
client registration, then an authorization-code exchange with PKCE against a
loopback redirect. The authorization URL is printed rather than opened. The
token is stored in \fI~/.mcpick/state/tokens.json\fR and attached automatically afterwards.
.TP
.B logout \fIserver\fR
Forget the stored token for a server; exits 1 when there is none.
.TP
.B agents
List the agents mcpick knows and how each one is reached.
.TP
.B restore
Put back every project file a session left rewritten, including sessions on
other hosts sharing the workspace. Launches do this automatically for sessions
on the same host whose process has ended.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-uid " ID"
Session id. Keys the saved selection and replaces \fB{UUID}\fR in the catalog.
Defaults to the hostname, which inside a container is the container id.
.TP
.BI \-\-file " PATH"
Catalog file. Defaults to
.I <root>/.mcp.yaml
or
.IR <root>/.mcp.json .
.TP
.BI \-\-agent " NAME"
Agent to render for. Defaults to the command name. The name is checked on
every command;
.B mcpick agents
lists them.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " NAME"
Use a named profile and skip the picker: yours first, then the catalog's;
\fBdefault\fR is the same as \fB\-\-all\fR (refused, with the way out, while
the catalog defines its own \fBdefault\fR). Servers this project does not
have are skipped with a warning.
.TP
.BI \-\-select " A,B"
Use exactly these servers and skip the picker.
.TP
.BI \-\-addr " HOST:PORT"
With
.BR serve ,
listen on HTTP instead of stdio. Only loopback addresses are accepted, because
the proxy has no authentication.
.TP
.BI \-\-home " DIR"
Where mcpick keeps everything it writes. Overrides \fB$MCPICK_HOME\fR; the
default is \fI~/.mcpick\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DURATION"
Per-server connect timeout, with its unit (\fI5s\fR, \fI2m\fR). Default 15s.
.TP
.B \-\-redact
With
.BR move ,
rewrite secrets as \fB${VAR:?export VAR}\fR references.
.B import
does so by default; the flag is accepted there and changes nothing.
With
.B \-\-yes
it is an error.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
With
.BR import ,
copy credentials as they are, with a warning; with
.BR move ,
write a server's credentials into the catalog as they are.
.TP
.B \-\-trust
With
.BR measure " and " doctor ,
approve the commands of stdio servers not yet trusted \(em what the catalog
says, without a prompt \(em and remember them as trusted for this project, in
.IR ~/.mcpick/state/trust.json .
Each command approved is printed on standard error before it runs.
Without the flag, such servers are skipped and named.
.TP
.B \-\-trust-catalog
With
.BR measure " and " doctor ,
trust this project's catalog as a whole, so that its remote servers are
measured unselected, placeholders and private hosts included; what is trusted
\(em the catalog file(s), each remote server with its URL and header names \(em
is printed on standard error first. The trust is kept in
.I ~/.mcpick/state/trust.json
under the project root and a hash of the catalog files' contents as they were
parsed, and lapses when a file changes. Stdio commands still need
.BR \-\-trust .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output for
.BR list ", " doctor ", " measure ", " agents " and " "profile list" .
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-last
Skip the picker and reuse the saved selection. When none was saved, a warning
says the agent will load no servers.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Select every server (never a hidden one) and skip the picker.
.TP
.B \-\-none
Select nothing and skip the picker.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage text.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH KEYS
In the picker:
.BR \[u2191]\[u2193] / jk
move,
.BR g / G
first and last,
.BR PgUp / PgDn
a page (the list scrolls with the cursor; see
.I config.yaml
below),
.B space
toggles (for claude, checking a server disabled in Claude Code re-enables it there at launch),
.B /
filters the list as you type,
.B m
measures every server in view (hidden ones only while their section is
unfolded; a stdio server's command runs only once trusted, the row says
\fBrun?\fR, and a second
.B m
on its row shows the command whole and asks; a remote server of the
repository's catalog that would send something of yours says \fBask\fR and
waits for a tick or \fBT\fR),
.B M
reviews every command not yet trusted and asks for all; on the screen
.B y
runs and trusts what is shown,
.B T
trusts the repository's catalog as a whole (it lists the file(s) and every
remote server the trust covers; on a trusted catalog it offers to untrust
it),
.B a
and
.B n
select all (never a hidden server) and none,
.B h
hides or unhides the server under the cursor,
.B H
unfolds or folds the Hidden section,
.B p
manages profiles (a screen of its own: \fB+\fR add, \fBc\fR copy, \fBr\fR rename,
\fBd\fR delete, \fBJ\fR/\fBK\fR move, \fBspace\fR toggle a server, \fBl\fR load,
\fBenter\fR launch, \fBesc\fR back);
.B s
and
.B l
save and load one,
.B +
adds a server,
.B d
deletes one,
.B v
moves one to another group (\fBp\fR project, \fBl\fR local, \fBu\fR user;
plugins are read-only),
.B enter
launches,
.B q
aborts. The key line under the list wraps over up to three lines; on a
terminal narrower than that it shows only the keys that fit. Every key works
whether or not it is shown.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <root>/.mcp.yaml
The catalog. Also read:
.IR <root>/.mcp.json .
.TP
.I ~/.mcpick/
mcpick's home, mode 0700; see \fB\-\-home\fR. It holds:
.RS
.TP
.I config.yaml
The user's defaults for the picker, optional and never written by mcpick:
.B max_rows
(default 10) is how many server rows are in view at once; the rest scroll.
An unknown key is ignored; a value that cannot be used is reported and the
default kept.
.TP
.I profiles.yaml
Your profiles: named selections, valid in every project.
.TP
.I selections/<workspace>-<hash>/<uid>.json
The saved selection: each checked server's name, origin and a hash of its
spec as written, never a value.
.TP
.I state/
OAuth tokens, measured context costs, the commands trusted for measuring
(\fItrust.json\fR: project, server name, a hash of command, arguments and
environment as written \(em never a value), the project catalogs trusted
(project and a hash of the catalog files' contents), and records for
restoring project files.
.TP
.I state/hidden/<workspace>-<hash>.json
The servers hidden with \fBh\fR, per workspace.
.TP
.I run/
Rendered configs and overlays. They contain expanded secrets, are mode 0600, and
are removed once the process that owns them has ended.
.RE
.TP
.I ~/.claude.json
Read for local- and user-scope servers.
.TP
.I ~/.claude/plugins/
Enabled plugins' servers are read so the selection can keep them;
\fB\-\-strict\-mcp\-config\fR drops them otherwise.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MCPICK_CONFIG
Set on the launched command, pointing at the rendered config.
.TP
.B MCPICK_HOME
mcpick's home, as for \fB\-\-home\fR.
.TP
.B MCPICK_DEBUG
When set, print the exact command mcpick runs, environment and real paths
included, just before launching it.
.TP
.B MCPICK_SERVE_ALLOW_REMOTE
Set to 1 to let \fBserve \-\-addr\fR bind a non-loopback address. Only behind
authentication of your own.
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
Where Claude Code's configuration, and so \fI.claude.json\fR and plugins, live.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Located for the agents configured through it (Muse, opencode).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error, or an unreachable or skipped server under
.BR doctor .
.TP
.B 128+n
The launched command died of signal \fIn\fR.
.TP
.B 130
The picker was aborted.
.PP
Otherwise, the exit status of the launched command.
.SH EXAMPLES
Pick interactively and launch Claude Code:
.PP
.RS
.B mcpick run claude
.RE
.PP
Reuse the last selection in a script:
.PP
.RS
.B mcpick -y run codex
.RE
.PP
Find out what is eating the context window:
.PP
.RS
.B mcpick measure
.RE
.PP
Give every agent one entry that never changes:
.PP
.RS
.B mcpick --profile review serve
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
The MCP specification at
.UR https://modelcontextprotocol.io
.UE .
